    {
      "id": "claim_4447c57c3df0493db1509e09bcc6a6d4",
      "statement": "zf_queue_watchdog.py is the queue watchdog: it auto-syncs open GitHub issues labeled zerofactory into active boards on a per-repo cooldown (a sync failure does not stamp the cooldown; synced issues park in triage assigned to human so no GPU tokens are spent on unvetted submissions), reaps stuck workers (reap_stuck_tasks), triggers run_dispatch_cycle, pulls check_stuck_tasks(include_blocked=True), and pulls get_stats; it emits a wakeAgent false signal when healthy (0 tokens) and a markdown alert when it finds a bottleneck.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/zf_queue_watchdog.py#L50-L266",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4764b10f3d6adea9e46ce074f0b0373497acfc6aaa9c1655ded8e5c15be60630:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c70c70668e24ac9883dcbd2487a2aeb",
      "statement": "zf_scanner_gate.py is the scanner wake-gate: it compares current Git HEAD/working tree against ~/.hermes/scanner_state.json and counts active pipeline tasks (running, todo) plus the board concurrency cap, emitting {\"wakeAgent\": false} to suppress the LLM scan when nothing material changed or the board is busy/cooldown, and {\"wakeAgent\": true} with pre-digested git context otherwise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
