    {
      "id": "claim_5f7b589c9aba416c9b4fff4d63e3c8de",
      "statement": "scripts/zf_openwiki_gate.py deterministically decides whether OpenWiki docs need a sync: it skips when openwiki/ is missing, the working tree is dirty, or (unless forced) an openwiki-titled task is already active in triage/todo/running/blocked; when HEAD has advanced past the last openwiki-touching commit it creates at most one P2 todo task for zf-builder via create_openwiki_task - through the dashboard create-task endpoint with a SQLite fallback that stamps the task with the JSON tags [\"automerge\", \"cat:documentation\"] - and never wakes an LLM (the script always exits 0).",
